From 999a1790f16c0a61540b7243106c69d5cca2809b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:40:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ggml-cpu, cuda: CPU reference fixes (CLAMP views,
 soft_max_back alias, get_rows_back bounds, AVX512-FP16 dot)

Four upstream CPU fixes. test-backend-ops judges every backend against the CPU reference,
so a wrong reference hides or fakes backend bugs; the CPU path is also served on CPU-only
hosts.
- CLAMP reads and writes through the source and destination strides (non-contiguous views);
  the CUDA backend now declares CLAMP only for contiguous rows and handles row strides (#29517).
  Conflict resolved by hand in ggml_backend_cuda_device_supports_op: our GGML_OP_TURBO_WHT case
  stays; upstream's moved GGML_OP_SCALE case is dropped because ours already lists SCALE above.
- soft_max_back gives the right output when dst aliases src1 (#27096).
- get_rows_back checks the row index bounds (#29575).
- f16 dot products accumulate in f32 on AVX512-FP16 (#29545). Inert on our X1 host: Zen 5
  has no AVX512-FP16.
Applied clean on our ggml-cpu hunks (ops.cpp, vec.*, simd-mappings.h). Protected CPU wins in
these files: anchor distances in cells/pw-disjoint-<merge-ready tip>.tsv.

Taken-from: ggml-org/llama.cpp@65840ed53c (#29517), ggml-org/llama.cpp@dd4c286f38 (#27096), ggml-org/llama.cpp@d3954b9324 (#29575), ggml-org/llama.cpp@284153e069 (#29545)
Origin: upstream-x1 lane PORT-SPEC P7
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED (correctness; CLAMP RED/GREEN, SOFT_MAX_BACK and GET_ROWS_BACK no-regression in MERGE-READY.md row P7)
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
